{"duration_api_ms":140653,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"4a0becc6-33b1-426b-b0e9-130562f4534d","total_cost_usd":0.4635733999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":46,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30456,"cache_read_input_tokens":1027487,"output_tokens":13616,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3916},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30456,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2239,"cache_read_input_tokens":53552,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1235,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1235},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":46,"outputTokens":13616,"cacheReadInputTokens":1027487,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30456,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4635733999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3916,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":28,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Implemented an Ansible playbook (run from node2, the only node with Ansible installed, targeting node1) that provisions a file-backed LUKS2 encrypted volume that auto-unlocks via a root-only keyfile at boot and auto-mounts at /srv/secure via crypttab + fstab. Verified auto-unlock/mount across a real reboot of node1, then completed the mandatory restart-evidence protocol on both node1 and node2, confirming boot-identity changes and full recovery of required services/data on each.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed node1 and node2: both Ubuntu 24.04; only node2 had ansible/ansible-playbook installed, so it was used as the Ansible control node targeting node1 over SSH\",\"Set up passwordless SSH from node2 to node1 using the cluster-provided CLUSTER_SSH_PRIVKEY/CLUSTER_SSH_PUBKEY\",\"Diagnosed and fixed node1's sshd failing to start (missing host keys) via ssh-keygen -A and systemctl enable --now ssh\",\"Verified Ansible connectivity from node2 to node1 with an ansible ping\",\"Wrote /root/ansible/encrypted-volume.yml on node2: generates a random keyfile at /etc/luks-keys/secure.key (mode 0400), creates a 512M backing file at /var/lib/secure-volume/secure.img, LUKS2-formats it with cryptsetup luksFormat, registers it in /etc/crypttab with the keyfile for automatic unlock, creates an ext4 filesystem on the mapped device, and registers /srv/secure in /etc/fstab (mount module, state=mounted) for automatic mounting\",\"Ran the playbook against node1 (ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini encrypted-volume.yml); verified the LUKS2 volume mounted at /srv/secure and wrote a test file to it\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, mount state, service state) for both node1 and node2\",\"Restarted node1 via a backgrounded systemctl reboot so the exec call could return before disconnection; polled until reachable again; confirmed boot_id changed (f9bf293d... -> ed87dad6...); confirmed via journalctl that systemd-cryptsetup@secure.service auto-unlocked the volume at boot and /srv/secure auto-mounted with the test file intact\",\"Restarted node2 the same way; polled until reachable; confirmed boot_id changed (489b0bb4... -> d323cb67...); confirmed ansible-playbook and the inventory/playbook files were intact and Ansible could still reach node1 (ping success) after the restart\",\"Re-verified node1's encrypted volume remained mounted with data intact after node2's restart, confirming end-to-end health of both nodes\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Encrypted volume mounted at /srv/secure on node1 (LUKS2, file-backed via loop device)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b1383ee293304527\",\"cmd-3ea5655500b84096\"],\"summary\":\"Ansible playbook run succeeded (17 tasks, 12 changed); post-run check shows /dev/mapper/secure LUKS2-active, loop-backed by /var/lib/secure-volume/secure.img, mounted ext4 at /srv/secure and writable\"},{\"requirement\":\"Volume unlocks and mounts on its own at boot (no manual intervention)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f9bf293d... N/A\",\"cmd-f3d60620425a4d8d\"],\"summary\":\"After a real reboot of node1, journalctl shows systemd-cryptsetup@secure.service automatically started and finished cryptsetup for 'secure' at boot, and /srv/secure was mounted with the previously written testfile.txt intact, with no manual cryptsetup/mount commands issued post-boot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Implemented using Ansible, from the correct control node\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2a250d3c202442e7\",\"cmd-f2d910a6a3ec4cde\",\"cmd-5fdb34789d8c4f77\",\"cmd-b1383ee293304527\"],\"summary\":\"node2 was identified as the only node with ansible/ansible-playbook installed; inventory and playbook were authored on node2 and ansible-playbook was executed from node2 against node1 over SSH\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 mandatory restart evidence: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d38a8b7fd3a341fb\",\"cmd-b6858d45de5b4d2a\",\"cmd-3ea5655500b84096\",\"cmd-5954bce34ef84668\",\"cmd-44803738f03c4612\",\"cmd-139752e56b3a434f\",\"cmd-cf19d1ec62194ac7\",\"cmd-f3d60620425a4d8d\"],\"summary\":\"Pre-restart baseline captured (boot_id f9bf293d..., mount/cryptsetup status, test file present); reboot acknowledged via backgrounded systemctl reboot; node became unreachable then responded again with boot_id ed87dad6... (changed); post-restart check confirmed cryptsetup auto-unlock service ran at boot and /srv/secure was remounted with data intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 mandatory restart evidence: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c384cacea5f943c5\",\"cmd-468765d7835c40ac\",\"cmd-ee12aeaf284d4253\",\"cmd-d6571f4db0a24723\",\"cmd-9daeaee6158641d5\",\"cmd-05365d95a0774dea\"],\"summary\":\"Pre-restart baseline captured (boot_id 489b0bb4..., ansible tooling present, ssh service state); reboot acknowledged via backgrounded systemctl reboot; node became unreachable then responded again with boot_id d323cb67... (changed); post-restart check confirmed ansible-playbook and playbook/inventory files intact and Ansible could still successfully ping/manage node1, and node1's encrypted volume remained healthy\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Implemented an Ansible playbook (run from node2, the only node with Ansible installed, targeting node1) that provisions a file-backed LUKS2 encrypted volume that auto-unlocks via a root-only keyfile at boot and auto-mounts at /srv/secure via crypttab + fstab. Verified auto-unlock/mount across a real reboot of node1, then completed the mandatory restart-evidence protocol on both node1 and node2, confirming boot-identity changes and full recovery of required services/data on each.","actions_performed":["Surveyed node1 and node2: both Ubuntu 24.04; only node2 had ansible/ansible-playbook installed, so it was used as the Ansible control node targeting node1 over SSH","Set up passwordless SSH from node2 to node1 using the cluster-provided CLUSTER_SSH_PRIVKEY/CLUSTER_SSH_PUBKEY","Diagnosed and fixed node1's sshd failing to start (missing host keys) via ssh-keygen -A and systemctl enable --now ssh","Verified Ansible connectivity from node2 to node1 with an ansible ping","Wrote /root/ansible/encrypted-volume.yml on node2: generates a random keyfile at /etc/luks-keys/secure.key (mode 0400), creates a 512M backing file at /var/lib/secure-volume/secure.img, LUKS2-formats it with cryptsetup luksFormat, registers it in /etc/crypttab with the keyfile for automatic unlock, creates an ext4 filesystem on the mapped device, and registers /srv/secure in /etc/fstab (mount module, state=mounted) for automatic mounting","Ran the playbook against node1 (ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini encrypted-volume.yml); verified the LUKS2 volume mounted at /srv/secure and wrote a test file to it","Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, mount state, service state) for both node1 and node2","Restarted node1 via a backgrounded systemctl reboot so the exec call could return before disconnection; polled until reachable again; confirmed boot_id changed (f9bf293d... -> ed87dad6...); confirmed via journalctl that systemd-cryptsetup@secure.service auto-unlocked the volume at boot and /srv/secure auto-mounted with the test file intact","Restarted node2 the same way; polled until reachable; confirmed boot_id changed (489b0bb4... -> d323cb67...); confirmed ansible-playbook and the inventory/playbook files were intact and Ansible could still reach node1 (ping success) after the restart","Re-verified node1's encrypted volume remained mounted with data intact after node2's restart, confirming end-to-end health of both nodes"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Encrypted volume mounted at /srv/secure on node1 (LUKS2, file-backed via loop device)","command_ids":["cmd-b1383ee293304527","cmd-3ea5655500b84096"],"summary":"Ansible playbook run succeeded (17 tasks, 12 changed); post-run check shows /dev/mapper/secure LUKS2-active, loop-backed by /var/lib/secure-volume/secure.img, mounted ext4 at /srv/secure and writable"},{"requirement":"Volume unlocks and mounts on its own at boot (no manual intervention)","command_ids":["cmd-f9bf293d... N/A","cmd-f3d60620425a4d8d"],"summary":"After a real reboot of node1, journalctl shows systemd-cryptsetup@secure.service automatically started and finished cryptsetup for 'secure' at boot, and /srv/secure was mounted with the previously written testfile.txt intact, with no manual cryptsetup/mount commands issued post-boot"},{"requirement":"Implemented using Ansible, from the correct control node","command_ids":["cmd-2a250d3c202442e7","cmd-f2d910a6a3ec4cde","cmd-5fdb34789d8c4f77","cmd-b1383ee293304527"],"summary":"node2 was identified as the only node with ansible/ansible-playbook installed; inventory and playbook were authored on node2 and ansible-playbook was executed from node2 against node1 over SSH"},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart evidence: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-d38a8b7fd3a341fb","cmd-b6858d45de5b4d2a","cmd-3ea5655500b84096","cmd-5954bce34ef84668","cmd-44803738f03c4612","cmd-139752e56b3a434f","cmd-cf19d1ec62194ac7","cmd-f3d60620425a4d8d"],"summary":"Pre-restart baseline captured (boot_id f9bf293d..., mount/cryptsetup status, test file present); reboot acknowledged via backgrounded systemctl reboot; node became unreachable then responded again with boot_id ed87dad6... (changed); post-restart check confirmed cryptsetup auto-unlock service ran at boot and /srv/secure was remounted with data intact"},{"requirement":"node2 mandatory restart evidence: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-c384cacea5f943c5","cmd-468765d7835c40ac","cmd-ee12aeaf284d4253","cmd-d6571f4db0a24723","cmd-9daeaee6158641d5","cmd-05365d95a0774dea"],"summary":"Pre-restart baseline captured (boot_id 489b0bb4..., ansible tooling present, ssh service state); reboot acknowledged via backgrounded systemctl reboot; node became unreachable then responded again with boot_id d323cb67... (changed); post-restart check confirmed ansible-playbook and playbook/inventory files intact and Ansible could still successfully ping/manage node1, and node1's encrypted volume remained healthy"}]},"ttft_ms":3316,"type":"result","duration_ms":169695,"uuid":"fa8ca6bd-2c21-4b65-8789-0175efa75f11","ttft_stream_ms"